Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: wait for an explicit SRAM provider

A DT with a separate SRAM region only maps the frame-engine registers
as the first Ethernet resource. If the SRAM provider is still probing,
defer Ethernet initialization instead of trying the legacy offset.

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -5210,6 +5210,12 @@
 			eth->sram_pool = of_gen_pool_get(pdev->dev.of_node,
 							 "sram", 0);
 			if (!eth->sram_pool) {
+				if (of_property_present(pdev->dev.of_node, "sram")) {
+					err = dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+							    "waiting for SRAM pool\n");
+					goto err_destroy_sgmii;
+				}
+
 				if (!mtk_is_netsys_v3_or_greater(eth)) {
 					err = mtk_setup_legacy_sram(eth, res);
 					if (err)
